1
00:00:14,648 --> 00:00:18,767
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:20,690 --> 00:00:22,277
[fzzt]

3
00:00:22,277 --> 00:00:26,033
Friggin' pseudo-wisdom... if you're not
insane, you're just ignorant.

4
00:00:26,669 --> 00:00:31,435
Okay, so these ARE teleporters.
That's helpful... I guess?

5
00:00:31,435 --> 00:00:34,019
Didn't do much for him, huh?

6
00:00:34,019 --> 00:00:40,072
I'm seeing an awful lot of dead researchers
still in their suits with blood everywhere.

7
00:00:40,072 --> 00:00:43,667
What kind of pressure would it
take to break the seals on their...?

8
00:00:44,208 --> 00:00:47,659
Are those bones I just saw
getting chucked out of there?

9
00:00:47,659 --> 00:00:52,175
Yeah! Shit! Those are meat chunks,
too! Somebody got hacked to pieces!

10
00:00:52,175 --> 00:00:57,490
Yeah, that's blood. That's red blood. 
The aliens bleed greenish-yellow.

11
00:00:57,490 --> 00:01:00,132
You can scratch
somebody else off the list.

12
00:01:00,132 --> 00:01:02,307
Oh, wow!

13
00:01:02,307 --> 00:01:04,726
Two stars!

14
00:01:04,726 --> 00:01:09,081
I'm surprised they can exist that
close without slamming into each other.

15
00:01:09,081 --> 00:01:14,818
This still explains nothing about
the gravity. Not a damned thing.

16
00:01:14,818 --> 00:01:17,938
I'm surprised I can breathe
with the gravity this low.

17
00:01:17,938 --> 00:01:22,035
Maybe there are some denser
gases trapping oxygen in somehow?

18
00:01:22,035 --> 00:01:24,498
This air DOES taste funny.

19
00:01:24,498 --> 00:01:25,300
[smacking lips]

20
00:01:26,439 --> 00:01:29,802
Ah, damn. It's one
of those bodybuilding aliens.

21
00:01:29,802 --> 00:01:33,154
How can they even get that
buff with the gravity this low?

22
00:01:33,154 --> 00:01:36,820
Maybe they wrestle with these tendrils
sticking out that try to whip you.

23
00:01:36,820 --> 00:01:38,367
I'm going to sneak up on them.

24
00:01:39,577 --> 00:01:42,194
Yeah, weren't expecting me, were you?

25
00:01:42,194 --> 00:01:44,249
I wouldn't expect me here.

26
00:01:44,249 --> 00:01:46,367
Here, this should give you
something to think about.

27
00:01:48,118 --> 00:01:49,338
Where did that come from?

28
00:01:49,338 --> 00:01:50,213
[explosion]

29
00:01:50,213 --> 00:01:52,100
It's a complete mystery.

30
00:01:54,023 --> 00:01:56,918
God, all that did was soften you up, too.

31
00:01:56,918 --> 00:01:58,405
So, what about this guy?

32
00:01:58,405 --> 00:02:00,801
Let's try this new weapon;
it shoots straight.

33
00:02:02,088 --> 00:02:03,841
Is this doing anything?

34
00:02:03,841 --> 00:02:05,367
He's just standing there.

35
00:02:06,489 --> 00:02:08,278
Oh, that worked pretty well.

36
00:02:08,278 --> 00:02:11,245
So, this gun actually DOES
something. That's great.

37
00:02:11,245 --> 00:02:14,614
I wonder why that guy didn't
fire at me or charge me.

38
00:02:14,614 --> 00:02:16,790
Maybe he can't see that far away.

39
00:02:16,790 --> 00:02:18,527
Or maybe he's still in training

40
00:02:18,527 --> 00:02:23,752
so the aliens on Earth really were the
best of the best, and this is what's left.

41
00:02:24,559 --> 00:02:28,134
Yeah, wow. You guys are
slow on the uptake, huh?

42
00:02:28,134 --> 00:02:30,028
Are you kidding me?

43
00:02:30,028 --> 00:02:31,857
I don't believe this.

44
00:02:31,857 --> 00:02:35,628
You're actually not trying to
attack me. This is a first.

45
00:02:35,628 --> 00:02:41,340
Okay, wow. You are doing everything
right for someone who wants to live.

46
00:02:41,340 --> 00:02:44,218
I wouldn't want to discourage
the learning process here.

47
00:02:44,218 --> 00:02:47,226
It looks like some of you can be
domesticated after all.

48
00:02:47,226 --> 00:02:51,529
Good! I mean, what's the point of being
king if you don't have any subjects?

49
00:02:51,529 --> 00:02:54,033
I feel like we're making
some real progress.

50
00:02:54,033 --> 00:02:57,454
Eventually, I'll need you to kill
your own kind who would harm me,

51
00:02:57,454 --> 00:02:59,100
but that's still a ways off.

52
00:02:59,461 --> 00:03:00,427
[vortigaunt charges up]
Nope!

53
00:03:01,161 --> 00:03:02,638
Okay, did you see that?

54
00:03:02,638 --> 00:03:05,990
This is what happens if you ever
raise your hand against me.

55
00:03:05,990 --> 00:03:08,615
I demand nothing less than
complete loyalty.

56
00:03:10,601 --> 00:03:14,611
Yeah, I can see some of you are
going to be faster learners than others.

57
00:03:14,611 --> 00:03:18,275
More ammo--how many
researchers WERE there?

58
00:03:18,275 --> 00:03:21,269
I think my theory is holding strong.

59
00:03:21,269 --> 00:03:21,968
Hm.

60
00:03:23,634 --> 00:03:27,500
Ah! Ah-ah! Okay, my foot's
stuck! My foot's stuck!

61
00:03:27,500 --> 00:03:29,156
Ah, that's better.

62
00:03:29,156 --> 00:03:30,868
Well, more water.

63
00:03:32,759 --> 00:03:34,917
Yeah, so there's nothing here.

64
00:03:34,917 --> 00:03:40,212
Y'know, I think I understand the invasion
now, because this place is trash.

65
00:03:40,212 --> 00:03:41,868
It's no contest.

66
00:03:43,559 --> 00:03:46,548
Earth kicks ass compared to this place.

67
00:03:46,548 --> 00:03:50,898
It's a series of SMALL islands
where you can fall to your death

68
00:03:50,898 --> 00:03:53,564
and the only way to get around
is a one-way teleporter.

69
00:03:53,564 --> 00:03:54,587
[vortigaunt charging up]
Shit.

70
00:03:54,587 --> 00:03:55,634
[vortigaunt bolt]
[shudder]

71
00:03:56,919 --> 00:03:58,639
Fucking insurgents!

72
00:03:58,639 --> 00:04:01,298
Well, that's to be expected at first.

73
00:04:01,298 --> 00:04:03,385
Two more for the pile, huh?

74
00:04:03,385 --> 00:04:05,888
How many is this, now?
Confirmed?

75
00:04:05,888 --> 00:04:08,150
And these are just the ones I'm finding.

76
00:04:08,150 --> 00:04:15,396
Oh, rockets! Yeah, this is my
new kingdom now. Classic conquest.

77
00:04:15,396 --> 00:04:18,477
You guys really should have done
your homework on humans

78
00:04:18,477 --> 00:04:21,185
before you decided to play this game.

79
00:04:21,185 --> 00:04:24,033
All right, well, you keep
pumping your...

80
00:04:24,846 --> 00:04:28,724
I have no idea what
the hell you are doing.

81
00:04:28,724 --> 00:04:31,987
Extracting the green venom of the land.

82
00:04:31,987 --> 00:04:37,249
It's not fuel. You guys don't
have vehicles or machines, really.

83
00:04:37,249 --> 00:04:41,549
If it wasn't for that metal armor I saw,
I'd suspect you don't even have industry.

84
00:04:41,549 --> 00:04:46,163
Let's face it, you're borderline savages
and you're lucky to have me here.

85
00:04:46,163 --> 00:04:49,382
I'm not here by choice, that's
for damned sure.

86
00:04:49,382 --> 00:04:52,935
But, now that I AM here, I'm going
to turn this place into something.

87
00:04:52,935 --> 00:04:54,888
I guess I'll have to start with just--

88
00:04:54,888 --> 00:04:56,471
[growling]

89
00:04:56,471 --> 00:04:57,602
Fuck, FUCK!

90
00:04:57,602 --> 00:04:59,912
THIS IS GOING TO SLOW DOWN THE PROGRESS!

91
00:04:59,912 --> 00:05:00,601
I NEED TO--

92
00:05:01,042 --> 00:05:02,188
DA-DAAH!

93
00:05:02,188 --> 00:05:04,265
YEAH, FOLLOW ME THROUGH HERE, BIG GUY!

94
00:05:04,265 --> 00:05:06,445
LET'S SEE YOU TRY AND SQUEEZE IN!

95
00:05:06,445 --> 00:05:08,560
Huh, this must be the lounge.

96
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:10,492
Yeah, he's not making it through this.

97
00:05:10,492 --> 00:05:12,577
The thing is, I knew this was
going to happen.

98
00:05:12,577 --> 00:05:13,832
Not this, specifically,

99
00:05:13,832 --> 00:05:16,222
but every other place
here has been its own hell.

100
00:05:16,222 --> 00:05:17,674
Why should this be different?

101
00:05:17,674 --> 00:05:19,106
What the hell?

102
00:05:19,106 --> 00:05:21,733
Where is this? I was there.

103
00:05:21,733 --> 00:05:22,807
Dah?

104
00:05:22,807 --> 00:05:25,274
So, this place grows
the green things now?

105
00:05:25,274 --> 00:05:27,030
The BIG green things?

106
00:05:27,030 --> 00:05:29,698
Yeah, see, this is exactly
what I'm talking about.

107
00:05:29,698 --> 00:05:34,504
I killed a handful of sleepy alien guards,
found some potential minions...

108
00:05:34,504 --> 00:05:36,196
That's not how this place works.

109
00:05:36,196 --> 00:05:37,649
It has to torment me.

110
00:05:37,649 --> 00:05:40,098
Every jump is a new hell.

111
00:05:40,098 --> 00:05:44,285
Although I may luck out on this one,
because I'm hoping his reptilian or...

112
00:05:44,285 --> 00:05:48,138
whatever brain has forgotten
I even exist by now.

113
00:05:48,138 --> 00:05:51,563
It has been a minute or so.
It should be enough time.

114
00:05:51,563 --> 00:05:52,483
Excellent!

115
00:05:52,483 --> 00:05:57,567
Yeah, you WATCH that entrance. If anything
comes here, it'll be through THAT entrance.

116
00:05:58,778 --> 00:06:03,158
Okay, gonna keep running,
just in case he gets bored.

117
00:06:03,158 --> 00:06:04,788
Bleh, bugs.

118
00:06:04,788 --> 00:06:08,406
Yeah, I am NOT over here.
Keep watching that entrance.

119
00:06:08,406 --> 00:06:12,274
Whoa, the darkness. I don't
trust the darkness.

120
00:06:12,274 --> 00:06:13,322
It's dark.

121
00:06:13,322 --> 00:06:15,409
BLAAAAAAAAAAH!

122
00:06:15,409 --> 00:06:16,825
I'm so slick.

123
00:06:16,825 --> 00:06:19,232
Jesus Christ! Are these islands alive?

124
00:06:19,232 --> 00:06:20,743
Is that how this works?

125
00:06:20,743 --> 00:06:24,746
Do they just keep growing
bigger and bigger things?

126
00:06:24,746 --> 00:06:27,180
Oh, some more red meat chunks.

127
00:06:27,180 --> 00:06:28,935
There goes another researcher.

128
00:06:28,935 --> 00:06:33,481
Okay, time for juggling lessons.
Your first lesson is to just grab the ball.

129
00:06:33,481 --> 00:06:34,641
Can you find it?

130
00:06:34,641 --> 00:06:35,755
Here's another one.

131
00:06:35,755 --> 00:06:37,152
Good, good.

132
00:06:37,152 --> 00:06:39,611
Just--no! Keep looking.

133
00:06:39,611 --> 00:06:42,231
Keep look--there you go.

134
00:06:42,231 --> 00:06:44,637
You need some more? Okay.

135
00:06:44,637 --> 00:06:46,775
Yeah, what's that? What's that?

136
00:06:46,775 --> 00:06:47,729
[explosion]

137
00:06:47,729 --> 00:06:49,896
It's amazing, that's what it is.

138
00:06:49,896 --> 00:06:51,133
Yeah, go find it.

139
00:06:54,702 --> 00:06:57,470
It's not there anymore, dumbasses.

140
00:06:57,470 --> 00:07:00,320
So, beyond the smaller
pink whipping things,

141
00:07:00,320 --> 00:07:03,765
we also have big green slamming things.

142
00:07:03,765 --> 00:07:09,234
Oh, I guess I'm out of the satchel charges
but those went to a good cause.

143
00:07:09,234 --> 00:07:12,876
Hey, you know what I haven't
been using? These tripmines.

144
00:07:12,876 --> 00:07:16,425
I think I know someone
who will fall for this.

145
00:07:16,425 --> 00:07:18,665
I thought these
could come in handy.

146
00:07:18,665 --> 00:07:20,234
Now, let's get his attention.

147
00:07:20,708 --> 00:07:23,289
Wow, I gave him too much credit.

148
00:07:23,289 --> 00:07:24,285
Yep! Yep.

149
00:07:24,285 --> 00:07:25,485
[explosion]

150
00:07:25,485 --> 00:07:31,491
That is music to my ears. The sound of
coming to terms with your own stupidity.

151
00:07:31,491 --> 00:07:33,582
Oh, the teleporter!

152
00:07:33,582 --> 00:07:36,081
So, the question is--DAMMIT!

153
00:07:36,081 --> 00:07:38,269
WHERE WERE YOU THIS WHOLE TIME?!

154
00:07:38,269 --> 00:07:40,255
SEE, THIS IS WHY I
HAVE TO USE THE TRIPMINES

155
00:07:40,255 --> 00:07:42,592
BECAUSE EVERY FUCKING
MOMENT IS LIKE THIS!

156
00:07:42,592 --> 00:07:46,236
I GET, WHAT, THIRTY SECONDS OF
CALM? THEN IT'S SCREAMING, KILLING,

157
00:07:46,236 --> 00:07:48,536
AND THEN IT'S HEAD EXPLOSION TIME!

158
00:07:48,536 --> 00:07:52,724
THERE'S NO TIME TO PLAN ANYTHING!
EVERYTHING'S JUST BLAAHHHBLAHHBLAAAH!

159
00:07:52,724 --> 00:07:56,323
See, I THOUGHT I'd catch a break
after I killed everything,

160
00:07:56,323 --> 00:07:59,075
but now I think the island might
just grow them forever.

161
00:07:59,075 --> 00:08:02,118
And ANOTHER dead researcher!
What a surprise!

162
00:08:02,118 --> 00:08:06,156
Yeah, this guy just fell and died on impact.
There's nothing more to this story.

163
00:08:06,156 --> 00:08:08,502
Well, he wasn't a total waste.

164
00:08:08,502 --> 00:08:10,158
So, do I go through?

165
00:08:10,158 --> 00:08:13,705
Well, they're all Hell, so I'm guessing
this one is a room full of bees.

166
00:08:13,705 --> 00:08:15,118
I'm about due for that.

167
00:08:15,118 --> 00:08:17,018
Yeah, bees! Let's do it.

168
00:08:17,018 --> 00:08:18,267
[fzzt]
Fuck.

